  "notes": "はらはら is an onomatopoeic word with two distinct uses.\n\nANXIOUS USE:\n- はらはらする{映画|えいが}: suspenseful movie\n- はらはら{ドキドキ}: nervous and excited\n\nFALLING USE:\n- {涙|なみだ}がはらはら{落|お}ちる: tears falling\n- {葉|は}がはらはら{散|ち}る: leaves fluttering down\n\nSIMILAR ANXIETY WORDS:\n- どきどき: heart pounding (excitement/nervousness)\n- ひやひや: feeling worried/chilled\n- そわそわ: restless, fidgety",
